> [!important] What this article actually is
> The cut is the **frame** around the sharper face you just produced in [[Part 2.0 - Fluid Dynamics & Oral Architecture|Part 2.0]]. ==The right cut is dictated by your hair biomechanics and skull geometry, not a magazine, not a Korean idol, not whatever the barber's last customer asked for.== This article maps your biology, then translates it into the cut you should be walking into the chair to request.

