## Styling vs retention: the clean line

> [!check] Two different problems, two different folders
> - **Retention (keeping the hair you have).** Owned by the [[Part 1.1 - What Actually Matters For Your Hair|Hair folder]]: DHT, follicle miniaturization, the topical/oral stack, dermatologist trichoscopy. ==Read that first if your hairline or crown is moving.==
> - **Styling (cutting the hair you have).** Owned here. The biomechanics of *how the hair you currently have can be shaped*.
>
> They feed into each other but they are not the same problem. A perfect cut on a thinning crown is wasted; a great retention stack with the wrong cut still looks bad.

